Introduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:4ddb37d0817fa30ef9958ee6bf41776d1d19a8d3ffcb09edb823142028d4ac66","file":"preprints/All-temperature-pressure-for-orthogonally-invariant-Ising-spin-glasses-September-25-2026/build/invariant-sk.tex","line":186,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"818e3a76d4a6e7928216dc8f30506aa087a12212580228d3638e1c8452b02419","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/All-temperature-pressure-for-orthogonally-invariant-Ising-spin-glasses-September-25-2026/build/invariant-sk.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:4ddb37d0817fa30ef9958ee6bf41776d1d19a8d3ffcb09edb823142028d4ac66","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/All-temperature-pressure-for-orthogonally-invariant-Ising-spin-glasses-September-25-2026/build/invariant-sk.tex#L186"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nLet $\\Lambda_N$ be deterministic real diagonal matrices whose empirical\nspectral measures converge weakly to a compactly supported probability\nlaw $\\mu$. Assume that their smallest and largest eigenvalues converge\nto the respective edges of $\\supp\\mu$. Let $U_N$ be Haar distributed\non $O(N)$, and define $P_N$ using the uniform spin probability in\nEquation~\\eqref{eq:pressure}. With $S$ and $G_1$ as in\nEquations~\\eqref{eq:S}--\\eqref{eq:G},\n\\begin{equation}\n \\lim_{N\\to\\infty}\\E P_N\n =\\lim_{N\\to\\infty}P_N\n =\\mathcal F(\\mu)\n :=\\inf_{p\\in\\cP}\\{S(p)+G_1(p)\\},\n \\label{eq:variational}\n\\end{equation}\nwhere the second limit holds almost surely. No independence of the\nmatrices $U_N$ across dimensions is required."}
